    "created_at": "2019-11-12T02:16:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-11-12T02:16:09Z",
    "body": "To protect users' privacy, WebHID should not expose stable device IDs (including USB serial number or Bluetooth device address) as these can be used for fingerprinting.\r\n\r\nInstead of exposing the serial number or Bluetooth address directly, perhaps we can hash information about the device with the origin URL to create a unique identifier for the origin/device pair. This would still allow an origin to recognize when a device is reconnected but would not be useful for tracking the user across origins.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
